---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — Cinematic Photo Editor';
const description = 'Cinematic Photo processes every image locally in your browser. Read our privacy policy to see exactly what data is, and is not, collected.';
const lastUpdated = 'August 7, 2026';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} path="/privacy-policy">
	<Navbar />
	<main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6">
		<span class="mb-4 block font-mono text-xs tracking-wide text-mute">PRIVACY POLICY</span>
		<h1 class="font-sans text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-4xl">
			Privacy Policy
		</h1>
		<p class="mt-3 font-mono text-xs text-mute">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

		<div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-6 text-base leading-7 text-body">
			<p>
				Cinematic Photo ("we", "us", "our") operates the website at cinematicphoto.com (the
				"Service"). This policy explains what information is, and is not, collected when you use
				the Service.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Your photos never leave your device</h2>
			<p>
				Cinematic Photo is a client-side application. When you drop, paste, or select an image,
				it is decoded and rendered entirely inside your own browser tab using the HTML Canvas
				API. Your photo is never uploaded, transmitted, or sent to our servers or any third
				party, and we have no ability to access, view, or store it. Closing or refreshing the tab
				removes the image from memory.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Information we do collect</h2>
			<p>
				Like most websites, our hosting infrastructure automatically logs standard technical
				information for security and reliability purposes, such as IP address, browser type,
				referring page, and request timestamps. We use this information only in aggregate to
				keep the Service running and secure, and we do not combine it with any image content,
				since none is ever sent to us.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Cookies and local storage</h2>
			<p>
				We do not use cookies or local storage for advertising or cross-site tracking. The
				Service may use browser storage solely to remember your editor preferences (such as your
				last-used preset) on your own device; this data is never transmitted to us.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Third-party services</h2>
			<p>
				Fonts and other static assets used by the Service are bundled and served directly from
				our own infrastructure rather than loaded from third-party font or script providers, so
				visiting the Service does not trigger requests to external tracking networks.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Children's privacy</h2>
			<p>
				The Service is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect
				personal information from children, consistent with the fact that no image or personal
				content is ever transmitted to us in the first place.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p>
				We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page
				with an updated "Last updated" date. Continued use of the Service after changes are
				posted constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Contact us</h2>
			<p>
				If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, visit our <a href="/contact-us" class="text-ink underline decoration-hairline-strong underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-ink">Contact Us</a> page.
			</p>
		</div>
	</main>
	<Footer />
</Layout>
